#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114970 :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-\\left(\\frac{1}{t-2}\\right)\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(-\\frac{1}{t-2}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114971 :question/id #uuid "3668609c-7f98-53ef-8aa7-6f9c3209dfee" :question/math-academy-id "e-2478" :question/problem "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $\\mathbf g (t) = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}\\ln   t \\\\ - t \\\\ {e}^{2 t}\\end{array} \\right]}$ and $u(t) = t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114972 :question/id #uuid "cbb15346-028c-59c0-9b20-cd2f408c3bcb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2479" :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114973 :question/id #uuid "228ae66f-9dad-5e6d-b405-9fbe62ecb7e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2480" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\\\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\\\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\\\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115760 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab8d5ef-8089-5175-ac19-96485f970f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299985} {:answer/id #uuid "2593ced8-b033-50da-a809-fe4246142ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}-t \\\\ {5}^{t}+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300141} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2fd8d0-a070-5db6-ae81-ced05e60caa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300253} {:answer/id #uuid "a6872ccd-6c7e-5432-936d-73672be13108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 12{t}^{2}+36 \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300801} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0c90f-dfca-51d0-b238-6b2f8dccaca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb0c90f-dfca-51d0-b238-6b2f8dccaca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300980} :answer-field/id #uuid "0034e2a3-f8d6-5a9e-9977-de07c87e0df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "39b28ff1-22a5-53af-8f2d-4d751a5c5d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-32286" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({5}^{t})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{bmatrix}+2t\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-16t \\\\ {5}^{t}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{5}^{t}\\cdot 2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0582802c-da60-55c8-b827-54e85f4c84ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+11{t}^{2}+12t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299957} {:answer/id #uuid "1b314b6c-c07c-5dd1-84b0-ae7405c80fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300087} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe098b-3d9f-5f11-993f-cab4cc8b011e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+14t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300454} {:answer/id #uuid "923e3fa5-b372-5604-81b4-5c6bf37d1887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300695} {:answer/id #uuid "e3888121-e3fe-55f8-8939-41b8db9b90ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3888121-e3fe-55f8-8939-41b8db9b90ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301095} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2898930-3fb5-5dee-8009-dea699857dae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a209f44d-4003-53ab-9d12-642d62514eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-32298" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "875b016f-e8c7-5871-b60a-8140d518ab7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24t^{3} - 2t - 6 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 42t + 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113551} {:answer/id #uuid "d3cb532f-811d-5a4d-a2ae-e7f634a389c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-42t - 20 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 24t^{3} + 2t + 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113552} {:answer/id #uuid "14263be6-a304-5e5d-b176-0b1171e81f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t + 20 \\\\ 8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113553} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6e72a8-69da-5220-88ac-e36adeb439a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 - 45t^{2} \\\\ 42t + 20 \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113554} {:answer/id #uuid "686fc5d6-9d73-5924-be7e-292fc0f83dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21t + 10 \\\\ 45t^{2} \\\\ -24t^{3} - 2t - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113555}] :answer-field/id #uuid "18574eab-4e64-5ca8-b34a-644e09dffb17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564ab4d2-73e6-558b-9af0-6f5fdd10eee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21t+10 \\\\ 45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390745} {:answer/id #uuid "08d9d97e-52f1-593e-bf6d-177ead5a4e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 42t+20 \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390746} {:answer/id #uuid "20623cb8-9b6d-552a-a5b9-c2b26e55fa4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-42t-20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 24{t}^{3}+2t+6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390747} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a88e03-753f-57ff-a632-12697f009654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-24{t}^{3}-2t-6 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ 42t+20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390748} {:answer/id #uuid "31d0af8e-650c-555d-ad59-94751914d534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d0af8e-650c-555d-ad59-94751914d534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390749} :answer-field/id #uuid "e189a085-a70a-5dfd-9709-316634fc8cbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "54437c76-a800-5517-9d6f-6a2f64f033aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-32353" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ where\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3{t}^{2} \\\\ t+4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} \\\\ 5t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6t \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4t \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6t & 1 & 0 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} & 5t\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}6t & 0 \\\\ t+2 & 5t\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}6t & 1 \\\\ t+2 & -2{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & t+4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4t & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}t+4 & 8 \\\\ -4t & 5\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}3{t}^{2} & 8 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}3{t}^{2} & t+4 \\\\ 1 & -4t\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5t \\\\ -30{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}37t+20 \\\\ 8-15{t}^{2} \\\\ -12{t}^{3}-t-4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}42t+20 \\\\ 8-45{t}^{2} \\\\ -24{t}^{3}-2t-6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041da615-473a-59b3-bd74-078cc5cac382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299946} {:answer/id #uuid "278a088d-66ff-5fc3-9def-6ae04de020b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300150} {:answer/id #uuid "67ce37ea-b2ab-5a58-86f8-69d3f8240639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300484} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0ec50a-1d0e-532d-ab8d-7cf840b59340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300820} {:answer/id #uuid "f2329096-2544-59c2-a74f-b394b5ad02bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "041da615-473a-59b3-bd74-078cc5cac382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299946} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a16360-6703-53e1-9901-03f44bb4aa65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0fd1def5-bd75-572c-939f-770f964a1db9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32498" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af26b52e-3810-51ea-bcac-9c8acc178d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15t^{4}, 9t^{2} - 4t^{3}, 12t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113575} {:answer/id #uuid "d89a1010-b029-5792-8386-b98d376ee90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t^{4},-t^{3}, 3t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113576} {:answer/id #uuid "0f6e6b35-ffb9-5f32-bb19-61dd743fdab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t,-1, 3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113577} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca95614-cc13-54c2-bac6-53445010da41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3t^{2}, 3 - t, 3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113578} {:answer/id #uuid "671b1663-a607-5e69-8ffb-86c468627dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5t^{4}, 3t^{2}, 4t^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113579}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c2951b-1c72-5268-832b-3b8119eb6b2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113574}] :question/id #uuid "e833221c-734a-52a6-a325-a894171df700" :question/math-academy-id "q-32501" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t) = ⟨3t^{2}, 3 - t, 3t⟩$ and $u(t) = t^{3}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "889f8013-9633-5472-a777-eca4c5e41e7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3{t}^{2}\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303308} {:answer/id #uuid "905a9185-fbd2-5d1d-b551-1887761f23f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358} {:answer/id #uuid "a284a409-3695-5062-bf15-c301f1626b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-2{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303458} {:answer/id #uuid "d627a4e8-bf07-5d84-bdda-4e0a8ab4c680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303786} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4b1cc6-899c-5984-bb4f-022c7fed3343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "905a9185-fbd2-5d1d-b551-1887761f23f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303358} :answer-field/id #uuid "1317e8fd-c944-52dc-90c8-a38a479a2646" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d41b7e5-385e-5e64-81bc-3cb7a2474527" :question/math-academy-id "q-32866" :question/problem "If $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,i+(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+12\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1-{u}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(12)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,i-2u\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t))\\,i-2(u(t))\\,j)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{3})\\,i-2({t}^{3})\\,j)\\cdot 3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{t}^{3}\\,i-6{t}^{5}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245c1016-9019-52b2-a26a-6ac0bf1d16f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302689} {:answer/id #uuid "3f808494-9cca-5881-91d6-e03f7e4beb4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302855} {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc6f526-3686-5eb6-a589-7d892e3678c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303726} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d545bc-df18-5895-b155-25b6a18a659c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} :answer-field/id #uuid "41acddb3-3570-5655-ad47-cf8c72851a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17db3926-f364-5101-a69e-c1d34df6ed10" :question/math-academy-id "q-33122" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad37ff22-26f6-50cd-9218-b742d80d0369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8, 1,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113623} {:answer/id #uuid "dce955db-803a-5eaa-8f40-9514713111b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 0, 48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113624} {:answer/id #uuid "51ccd42e-d655-5177-a52d-935b7434f13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24, 3, 36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113625} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3be7aa-7f8b-5864-bdec-850462bcfb32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6, 0, 24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113626} {:answer/id #uuid "7a69da90-0384-583a-882a-0121d8fd94a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 3,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113627}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7ff49b-47bd-5f8b-a647-fae948868913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113622}] :question/id #uuid "a73b3659-30e4-5063-9479-5d3e2f941065" :question/math-academy-id "q-33143" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h}(t) & =⟨2{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t-3,\\hspace{0.222em}8+{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}+2t,\\hspace{0.222em}8,\\hspace{0.222em}2{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b40cf7a-fa7c-5050-b2e9-e2f7ba04828a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259977} {:answer/id #uuid "175264bb-f389-5869-951c-76cc68611d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260079} {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} {:answer/id #uuid "395164b8-31dd-524a-ab0d-565231ea5e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260386} {:answer/id #uuid "fce4134e-0fcd-5135-8ad0-7457cadd83ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eac5ff3-a989-52ce-a1dc-128ad336dc00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "65ab200e-3546-5bdf-91aa-8c6105b3b769" :question/math-academy-id "q-128137" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}$ at $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3(t+1)},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-3{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{3(t+1)}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(0)-3g(0))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(0)-3{g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+1}},\\,3(0)^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{0+1}⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3(0+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e9deaa-32e1-5ea1-8ac9-d0b7cec610d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260804} {:answer/id #uuid "786ded6e-e2cc-5b48-8f31-f18de453ddf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260928} {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} {:answer/id #uuid "bee221f3-f2b6-59f9-bc02-f014daed57c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\pi ,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261564} {:answer/id #uuid "e98af580-cfca-5b9f-a49f-53c6b11bb2c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,4\\pi ,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f0cbd8-ad26-5506-89ef-79e23f60a2f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d61cd968-7256-5d6b-88d3-edf46ce0ae3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128452" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)-{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8\\sqrt{3-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-1,\\,2\\pi t,\\,-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(-1)-g(-1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(-1)-{g}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-(-1)}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ),\\,\\frac{1}{(-1)}⟩-⟨2(-1)-1,\\,2\\pi (-1),\\,-2(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-2,-\\pi ,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2\\pi ,-2⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f2fbae0-f6d7-546c-827c-374938408879" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260853} {:answer/id #uuid "71402034-ff9c-5e89-8506-730d8d44e9b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260867} {:answer/id #uuid "92984806-47e0-5523-b871-7b33717a7972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261148} {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} {:answer/id #uuid "fc50c87f-1bce-55e7-87f1-cf2d24533ccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a5d268-0bb4-5a51-b597-b06cd810f718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "143a675a-6cf0-552b-b195-46b4f34bf0d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128458" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{3+t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2t-3 \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ (t+1)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have \n \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+5{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2\\sqrt{3+t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+t}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1)^{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 2(t+1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence , we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(1)+5g(1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(1)+5{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-1) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2(1) \\\\ 2(1+1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f72b45b-32fa-5846-8f1b-fc09e15dd9af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260433} {:answer/id #uuid "77fb7a60-00b8-5218-9921-1f39feba326a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260924} {:answer/id #uuid "8d76152a-5288-544b-8dea-d4af8e174c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261113} {:answer/id #uuid "9d391b58-7274-5c35-8b7b-6c8acc0893a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261234} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e6e1bb-d01a-512c-97e8-610afd3f35d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6e6e1bb-d01a-512c-97e8-610afd3f35d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262034} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8f8745-4998-5897-9f4a-16c888b2f208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "345451d2-c71d-53b2-ba4b-9528a0f7f324" :question/math-academy-id "q-128473" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bb14e6-4804-566e-8ba1-cd6661d9e27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259955} {:answer/id #uuid "42ea72dd-3fe1-52af-a8c1-ff45b339f5ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2},\\,5\\sqrt{t},\\,3{t}^{2}\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260458} {:answer/id #uuid "a0962aa2-e4c4-5ed5-a38d-661cd0c6397f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261270} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b920ba-40d7-52c4-8b7d-9ba1225aab16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261273} {:answer/id #uuid "b0145eca-83e8-5b7f-93f4-8603d5621461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,2t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08bb14e6-4804-566e-8ba1-cd6661d9e27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259955} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f997dd1-3807-549f-be54-0c6c67a6ae0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f6ebbf1-7ac8-5d1e-b90d-f43ce0433207" :question/math-academy-id "q-128477" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $u(t)=2\\sqrt{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{t}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4t\\sqrt{t},\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩+⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{t},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,5t\\sqrt{t},\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f663231-0ba7-5629-be71-2d2ead4d3723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-2,\\,-t,\\,t-2{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260431} {:answer/id #uuid "586b07f8-82bd-52eb-bdf1-cf3065aede5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+t,\\,2+t,\\,t+3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260631} {:answer/id #uuid "5fa8b05a-0de5-5531-8860-7f42d89a207b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-1,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260700} {:answer/id #uuid "97d18fc2-232e-5625-a79a-3bb31bd8b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261191} {:answer/id #uuid "d02647d8-a2fc-5aa9-bdb0-fd91b0c9215c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,-2{t}^{2},\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97d18fc2-232e-5625-a79a-3bb31bd8b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261191} :answer-field/id #uuid "151308c3-28fc-5bd3-ab19-c0fac585d178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "28487445-4637-5ffc-a325-dcbc682a33b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128479" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=1-t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =(1-t)⟨1,\\,1,\\,2t⟩-⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-t,\\,1-t,\\,2t-2{t}^{2}⟩-⟨t,\\,1+t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2t,\\,-2t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ff800d3-9925-5a1f-9bfc-6f9a48992b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260023} {:answer/id #uuid "29455431-af0d-5c43-a32c-24a26aa144f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260237} {:answer/id #uuid "311ab69a-928a-588d-9516-989f0c7c8e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260316} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8672a2-39a1-59bb-bc5c-8f90cd8fffd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260968} {:answer/id #uuid "93a8bad7-ecb6-5eb1-b599-4e63c3bbc5da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "311ab69a-928a-588d-9516-989f0c7c8e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260316} :answer-field/id #uuid "b68cb0b5-e8bb-527b-ae06-1c4fc55256df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c82af0d-c66c-5c8e-bb72-c5cfe1d3d608" :question/math-academy-id "q-128481" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a95b330-bb37-5112-b358-d912678bfc92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-t},\\,2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260400} {:answer/id #uuid "3e40b650-d8f4-57b2-907a-ecc623553ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t},\\,1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260423} {:answer/id #uuid "584135ce-ff8c-5cfb-be88-d839ebd7fb66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,{t}^{2}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260627} {:answer/id #uuid "701fd60a-c439-5e95-8ef7-d416b3758579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260860} {:answer/id #uuid "91c2f62a-23b7-59f8-9406-a77293ea9045" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-t,\\,2(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "701fd60a-c439-5e95-8ef7-d416b3758579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260860} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4ba4514-1f97-55cf-8137-48dda5c44cce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b459a16-1ddd-5fd7-b65f-64ec230fc1a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128485" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩+t⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t,\\,0⟩+⟨2t{e}^{-t},\\,4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{-t}-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t+4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d174aa-f9dc-519a-9e06-114c43894f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260180} {:answer/id #uuid "3661956c-4318-53fc-ab1c-41b76ef2b5bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260361} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0b2ee6-a1be-5aa4-868f-eda5b7d48d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260421} {:answer/id #uuid "d905812a-aaa1-5520-a293-216f1bd217d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261788} {:answer/id #uuid "fe28d3f4-7453-5eff-b63a-74f22f763357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe28d3f4-7453-5eff-b63a-74f22f763357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262104} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee0348a2-9e74-50f7-b367-df15c4e87791" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "00d88c3d-4bf1-50cd-93ca-fa7a07f78778" :question/math-academy-id "q-128563" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡u⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{2},$ then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,\\frac{1}{u},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u(t)),\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡(u(t))⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =⟨2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t{sec}^{2}⁡({t}^{2})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec05e04-f32a-5c49-a611-64176e13f05b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260138} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9ab6cf-1068-58d5-b0b8-4a57bc298465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261513} {:answer/id #uuid "d90f7345-ceb8-589a-8010-5de21965e39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261791} {:answer/id #uuid "df0b1a54-2ab7-50ca-bfb6-a3573529b3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261845} {:answer/id #uuid "e0390c70-7361-56c3-82ff-71cd8dcf9d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba9ab6cf-1068-58d5-b0b8-4a57bc298465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261513} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a258e83-dd78-569c-a860-539082a16c70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "66bcb8b8-02ef-54f0-8d3f-6e0da42ee49d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128572" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(6)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2({e}^{t}) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262925 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b93f617-87e0-5210-be19-97741891991d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260262} {:answer/id #uuid "3580541f-830f-598a-a783-88fec72dde5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260354} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a9d477-3e12-5007-82c2-dfea71222f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,t,\\,3t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261312} {:answer/id #uuid "af3b5194-5a5b-5ac7-8760-ba017f3228d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261421} {:answer/id #uuid "baf1879f-f001-552d-a8d4-7e78fda261e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3580541f-830f-598a-a783-88fec72dde5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260354} :answer-field/id #uuid "f56a291e-1a05-5ec8-8e7b-40a05867d66d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "995d1b63-3fd5-54e1-bbec-560efe7ac735" :question/math-academy-id "q-128586" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $v(t)=2t.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩+⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c405b6-8e2c-5767-9204-4bdb2fa66d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{3},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259956} {:answer/id #uuid "6e532cd0-5a24-5b51-bb5f-bc2c5bfaaba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260847} {:answer/id #uuid "6fce5174-2553-542e-83df-f8d10e69e544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{4},\\,3{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260856} {:answer/id #uuid "9d94ed22-c699-542a-beb8-1d79f82bd0b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{2},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261240} {:answer/id #uuid "bca4179f-3737-54cf-b42b-7f31dd9110b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca4179f-3737-54cf-b42b-7f31dd9110b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261540} :answer-field/id #uuid "74146d36-b0eb-5ca0-9527-75ddfa0fc7f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e2c98f03-8eb1-5c14-ba1a-38fe2722976d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128587" :question/problem "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(ug(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩+3{t}^{2}⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩+⟨3{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2f0c39-14ec-595e-a4ae-3b0e0f36d00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{t+1},\\,2,\\,4{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260134} {:answer/id #uuid "37f837c5-b882-5c17-be53-31f9d462ba0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,-3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260372} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2ab197-ba6d-56ea-b802-ada707de7359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-2,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260980} {:answer/id #uuid "87cd4c98-ec33-54b2-a15c-b9f4c0dc1eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261057} {:answer/id #uuid "b3735980-9110-5643-906a-122ec95305f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3735980-9110-5643-906a-122ec95305f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261458} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e222c03-3a8a-5590-9dfe-dfec486e1c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d768288b-91a5-51ed-b29b-7650008bff18" :question/math-academy-id "q-128894" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩$ and $v(t)={e}^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩+{e}^{t}⟨{e}^{t+1},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,-1,\\,2{e}^{3t}⟩+⟨{e}^{2t+1},\\,1,\\,{e}^{3t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2t+1},\\,0,\\,3{e}^{3t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6f401a-1af1-5902-8ecf-8f185e9e12da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300092} {:answer/id #uuid "3d489b9a-c7ce-5bb5-9c1e-bb2fb01f89fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300261} {:answer/id #uuid "7630cb27-95dd-503c-86cf-d9a96b47156b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300546} {:answer/id #uuid "875ea830-aed4-554d-85ae-d63a3f76be32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} :answer-field/id #uuid "610d999b-36f3-554e-acdc-7690f0627a2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5ce8c747-438b-5a4a-8cfe-ec69b8a216ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-32499" :question/problem "Differentiate $2g(t)-h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t-3,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have\n\n$$\n(2g(t)-h(t))^{′}=2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2g(t)-h(t))^{′} & =2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6-(-1),\\,-4t-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d6a0cfc-1fdb-5a5d-8094-0fa7eb47f049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300585} {:answer/id #uuid "85523c05-e822-5ae2-b93d-18c8dfd83b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t\\,i+4t\\,j+4t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300628} {:answer/id #uuid "9570fd04-d2da-5722-889f-b628cb28acf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t\\,i+8t\\,j+12t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300711} {:answer/id #uuid "95853092-5e55-5770-9781-01cbd398a49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}i+2{t}^{2}\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300713} {:answer/id #uuid "a47237b6-6c15-5c8f-a39e-9bcc3a189feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d6a0cfc-1fdb-5a5d-8094-0fa7eb47f049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300585} :answer-field/id #uuid "68503596-a623-58aa-b2ac-c212d77d484d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5d2dc74e-c392-56dc-bab3-713a1d0cef87" :question/math-academy-id "q-32502" :question/problem "If  $f(u)=u\\,i+2u\\,j+3u\\,k$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}u\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}2u\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}3u\\,k \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+3\\,k \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j+3\\,k)2t \\\\  & =2t\\,i+4t\\,j+6t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302172 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2a4bfc-5f35-5ae9-a821-d3bce3a9c6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300442} {:answer/id #uuid "7a714d86-ceb0-57c7-a902-31a1b72e5f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300565} {:answer/id #uuid "87911319-25bb-5038-bd99-46da453974fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300646} {:answer/id #uuid "9e03f1e2-6fb5-5862-a16d-73e44a1f2e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4e2c0bf-91fb-53b7-a114-172b95036f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f67b45fc-cd86-5ee0-8299-de9e4060f565" :question/math-academy-id "q-32503" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aa27233-ccd6-5600-aa83-1e26fdfc1d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300082} {:answer/id #uuid "4659858f-2f59-59af-8140-bdeb6a985b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300314} {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb3dee-7a8c-53dc-9b4d-450bf35eee82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300366} {:answer/id #uuid "847f2c4d-2f3a-5e6c-b901-f7b8090c71a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{t}^{4}+50{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300621} {:answer/id #uuid "c35962a3-cffe-5d24-bfef-7b8c30272350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb3dee-7a8c-53dc-9b4d-450bf35eee82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300366} :answer-field/id #uuid "7edc08bf-eaa3-58b5-8650-9797f1b61df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "19486880-810b-5bd6-a22c-f282191bb018" :question/math-academy-id "q-32804" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+5\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2})\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(10t)\\,k \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2t\\,i+(0)j+(10)\\,k \\\\  & =12t\\,i+10\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(12t\\,i+10\\,k)\\cdot (2{t}^{3}\\,i-2t\\,j+(1+5{t}^{2})\\,k)+(6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k)\\cdot (6{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+10t\\,k) \\\\  & =(12t\\cdot 2{t}^{3}+0\\cdot (-2t)+10\\cdot (1+5{t}^{2}))+((6{t}^{2})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(10t)^{2}) \\\\  & =24{t}^{4}+0+10+50{t}^{2}+36{t}^{4}+4+100{t}^{2} \\\\  & =60{t}^{4}+150{t}^{2}+14\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb30d24-e5fa-5ff3-b793-37ff771c864a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}+6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300014} {:answer/id #uuid "26a29261-3951-5f05-aa91-50190f871a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300147} {:answer/id #uuid "54f4bc9d-9659-533f-bcde-0d8203d7cee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300401} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8ad0ce-f737-58e3-9a2a-e7e35fa2da52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300509} {:answer/id #uuid "849785f2-76ee-5ce4-8123-ab009fa163a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "849785f2-76ee-5ce4-8123-ab009fa163a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300624} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d48190f-ac7f-5e0c-a042-b8a82e88e0a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "38bbc30d-2715-5fd5-8cc3-adae49e8b272" :question/math-academy-id "q-32835" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write: \n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,6t⟩\\cdot ⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,2t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩+⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =(2\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1)+0\\cdot (2t)+6t\\cdot ({t}^{3}-1))+((2t)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2+0+6{t}^{4}-6t+4{t}^{2}+4+9{t}^{4} \\\\  & =15{t}^{4}+6{t}^{2}-6t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302435 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "062642b3-def7-5feb-8f41-08b7e4a64ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299962} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd64be2-30aa-5f51-a354-0c648f752da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300175} {:answer/id #uuid "73e23c91-17b0-5276-ba29-6df6883eb88f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300538} {:answer/id #uuid "c02fe4ca-cc73-5724-8dbb-64c1e0b63d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300925} {:answer/id #uuid "e88569b0-7f63-5ac6-b787-2020ea0b2e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e23c91-17b0-5276-ba29-6df6883eb88f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300538} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f006c5-3411-58f0-9d06-d677c36cb1c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "829808f0-e345-5eeb-99ad-5982ddad6fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32837" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+4\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+8t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\,i+2j+8\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+2j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0) & ={f}^{″}(0)\\cdot f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)\\cdot {f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\,i+2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\,i+({0}^{2}-2)\\,j+4(0)^{2}\\,k)+(3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k)\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (-i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016435a7-09df-59ed-8e52-f08535ec47e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302457} {:answer/id #uuid "32d17b7e-35d0-57c3-ba6d-1d89eb61e334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302768} {:answer/id #uuid "39e3dc14-bd57-5747-9a00-81c2814bbcbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302817} {:answer/id #uuid "6f93626f-cc40-5170-9705-d920aff7ec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303139} {:answer/id #uuid "a07903a9-95bb-5a12-97e9-bc7e59ec2065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2u\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f93626f-cc40-5170-9705-d920aff7ec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303139} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f7d124-041e-581f-adbe-c38cf8ebd23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8d3c1bb9-bc23-5441-85c4-926900a42dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32860" :question/problem "If $g(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ 5 \\\\ {u}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$, then  $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,5\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{u(t)} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u(t)\\end{bmatrix}{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029ffd0e-a808-5dc2-b75a-236b9d62df96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302470} {:answer/id #uuid "3d48b11a-9299-5f42-982a-2d1e1bb0cbae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302838} {:answer/id #uuid "440997d6-7fcd-5bd7-8476-b139f1366f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302887} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9318c8-6af1-5310-8e35-7ffb568cb102" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303126} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c80301-2671-501b-931c-8779d0c7081d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,{e}^{-4t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "440997d6-7fcd-5bd7-8476-b139f1366f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302887} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b5f082-25b7-5165-91ab-092341e9996d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53be4820-056b-50b8-b65a-84c0096afdb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-32869" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{u}⟩$ and $u(t)={e}^{2t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}0,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\left(\\frac{1}{u}\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}(t)}⟩{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{({e}^{2t})^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{4t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41126a54-8e43-5888-909a-644b0fa2584e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302866} {:answer/id #uuid "89b704e5-d1d6-5b5f-b7c9-5e1091541afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303316} {:answer/id #uuid "989a417c-9f9c-520c-a1ca-b762a6d26b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303404} {:answer/id #uuid "a7aa4261-f293-5497-8bca-0be34ef4c95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303485} {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb6aef3-3384-522e-8f0d-b00fdf0b7619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c3147421-0af0-52d2-8626-d7432dc16238" :question/math-academy-id "q-33123" :question/problem "Differentiate $2f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(j-\\,k) \\\\ g(t) & =(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}1\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)+3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383ec955-af72-5aeb-813c-b7e9c4f5d6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302802} {:answer/id #uuid "66c922b2-90d5-511b-af8e-8bcfb11c92dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303077} {:answer/id #uuid "ef13717f-b212-5a08-aa3b-404f5a84709d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303955} {:answer/id #uuid "f38486c3-26cc-5013-9bbc-fc27b9c0dbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303984} {:answer/id #uuid "f827b8fb-15b2-57b4-b157-dc8224f13cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef13717f-b212-5a08-aa3b-404f5a84709d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303955} :answer-field/id #uuid "181930e4-89b2-5460-a910-ab0f457c2a21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30bcefa5-8086-5c62-ab2e-eb5b519248a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-33260" :question/problem "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b7a747-95ef-5439-8a0d-a5d0bc972bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305178} {:answer/id #uuid "071d818f-582a-511b-8e1a-da0e02e5e527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305217} {:answer/id #uuid "39c46305-4821-5d35-b86b-257d73a82b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305701} {:answer/id #uuid "60474004-6f0b-518e-bd0a-d1fd73598741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306080} {:answer/id #uuid "79db6f46-1f9b-5903-82ac-d8484423c92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60474004-6f0b-518e-bd0a-d1fd73598741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306080} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7db7aa7-b12e-53b6-82a4-b2d5f20ca566" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8a9de11b-dc85-5ae6-9285-a0d6cc055460" :question/math-academy-id "q-33336" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{1}{t}\\,j+t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =t\\,i+\\frac{1}{t}\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)\\,j+1\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j+k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =1\\,i+\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j+k)\\cdot (t\\,i+\\frac{1}{t}\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+\\frac{1}{t}\\,j+t\\,k)\\cdot (i-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{t}\\,k) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot t-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{t}\\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right)+t\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}+1 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+2-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df4d9e4-5aab-5758-b6bf-f561a4a5bc13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} {:answer/id #uuid "567f9cec-a4ac-5823-9ae9-ff55dac8a4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305989} {:answer/id #uuid "858bfa6f-4a26-5ea8-bf05-c82787e1d16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306424} {:answer/id #uuid "db9b03e9-0749-562a-b299-e3af23995ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307187} {:answer/id #uuid "f30b8be4-1b5a-550e-a1eb-f3bf87eff617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df4d9e4-5aab-5758-b6bf-f561a4a5bc13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305590} :answer-field/id #uuid "843487b0-a154-5051-ab18-86349bd94dcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "360e7d39-e582-5724-9fad-4481a2f3b45b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33446" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" :question/worked-solution "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}\\right)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac5b001-3222-5f20-9cfa-a6a178edbcf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336134} {:answer/id #uuid "43211d42-ef9b-5294-9784-f61afc4354fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336665} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0b1790-c755-5de3-8e68-28d3776dc12c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336737} {:answer/id #uuid "adc3c998-c9bf-5aa6-bbfb-3bb4b5b897c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337591} {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6a4498-4274-5a8f-a340-b4c6887cef4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bba82f4d-eee0-52ff-96d4-e8a4604b03f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70681" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1e76c73-4dda-53f0-be01-314247fc0ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337755} {:answer/id #uuid "e205aafb-db03-50ba-a9cf-e2e2bf49b182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337999} {:answer/id #uuid "ecde76ee-f28d-580d-9db5-9149c8cdbb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338099} {:answer/id #uuid "ed54e252-e227-5dc6-9931-79218dd313f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338102} {:answer/id #uuid "fff0d9bc-2402-5c81-84fb-e6405699052c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1e76c73-4dda-53f0-be01-314247fc0ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337755} :answer-field/id #uuid "936abeb3-90ac-5f81-aede-5e4550d7f9f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f31a5c94-f740-5b67-b455-a131169207f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-70685" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fe3261-4909-5096-b5e1-f76176162165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336357} {:answer/id #uuid "712f0496-f2a0-5abd-b4c8-73de224a043e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337041} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d1eff-3823-57a2-bdcc-d1c03822f1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337176} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdbc4b9-9974-5b9e-acea-527268caf412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337700} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dacc4f-6a8e-538f-a3d3-2b9938bc01da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d1eff-3823-57a2-bdcc-d1c03822f1b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337176} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e58e48c-9dd0-5119-9cc7-b119ae414c42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "caf13fa2-de78-52bc-ba1b-170f27934a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71225" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=2t-3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{bmatrix}+(2t-3)\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ae2bca-e693-5057-b172-8c6834c9305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336046} {:answer/id #uuid "3b032cb3-2592-5b9d-9061-33bfc2a7a76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336587} {:answer/id #uuid "5f14825a-b07a-50fe-8e14-408159c0bd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336895} {:answer/id #uuid "c77c316d-ec73-593a-b180-6b62e7becd6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}({t}^{2}+{t}^{3}){e}^{t} \\\\ 4t \\\\ {t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337802} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ec56e9-e917-5a25-81bb-919f520b8be7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(1-{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 8t \\\\ (t+{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b032cb3-2592-5b9d-9061-33bfc2a7a76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336587} :answer-field/id #uuid "d96b1280-82f4-5da6-a8ce-bc175b6dad01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9e0b692-7256-5bab-8d93-e2cff98bff96" :question/math-academy-id "q-71230" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2t\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+{t}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2353783-74f2-5934-bfba-3023b84ceef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373120} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe13228-3768-591d-9f6a-24b6e1eb93a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373121} {:answer/id #uuid "72be2dff-28b8-52fc-9246-55ec88b83a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373122} {:answer/id #uuid "61bb40c2-9ecf-585d-b790-f34cbaa9de79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373123} {:answer/id #uuid "243cbcf4-b0d8-5b82-ad87-04f8e247276b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ {e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72be2dff-28b8-52fc-9246-55ec88b83a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373122} :answer-field/id #uuid "91cea048-4a27-504b-b918-c58dbf7788d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df22d5ba-b0c3-58b3-a878-bdf0e607174d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71222" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {e}^{u}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=4t-3,$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ {e}^{u}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-3)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ {e}^{u(t)}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ {e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a768cdba-762c-56fa-9c5a-e7c147a0278c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387861} {:answer/id #uuid "308ec3e7-64ed-53d8-95f6-4019058929dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387862} {:answer/id #uuid "c6683669-2c03-5f5d-9b0c-ade45ed8142d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387863} {:answer/id #uuid "76309ab8-5db5-5655-9fd2-0aa6a5daad69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387864} {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865} :answer-field/id #uuid "437f6985-a5fd-5604-8d5e-718379fa984b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a16c9dc1-0124-53fd-9b82-d496e53dbcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387868} {:answer/id #uuid "f616ca61-be0f-5144-b6c8-08476269dd60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387869} {:answer/id #uuid "309785b0-a118-5c93-829d-4b1bec8533d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387870} {:answer/id #uuid "a99725fb-c5ed-5e02-9f65-da1970e78632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,7,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387871} {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872} :answer-field/id #uuid "f682f616-b62a-5bba-8f73-0577cd6f697d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "998ff16d-b6a6-5973-8b01-9ee14eef7c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-128144" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-2{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(1)-2g(1))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(1)-2{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =⟨2(1),\\,\\frac{1}{1},\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩-2⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}},\\,3(1)^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-2⟨1,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb777dec-9a7d-5180-aed9-ced5ab07530a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387882} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8a4ef6-8622-5fc7-a443-ab29bf7a715d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387883} {:answer/id #uuid "36b3f452-c970-515d-8ba9-3c73dc8dd6d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(1-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387884} {:answer/id #uuid "630e0a54-6d2c-509b-a321-bd2d769d03ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ t{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387885} {:answer/id #uuid "4add20c5-e378-54d6-93c5-3fa122ce7d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb777dec-9a7d-5180-aed9-ced5ab07530a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387882} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e6c637-4501-56e5-b8a0-e8e26bd20e58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3b0680d9-f905-5e2d-ad7e-963cf0c87370" :question/math-academy-id "q-128488" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={e}^{-t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})=-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}-{t}^{3}{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{-t}(3-t) \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32740510-69e4-53a8-9cf8-9c29535d9249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,i-4{e}^{-2t}\\,j-2{e}^{-3t/2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387903} {:answer/id #uuid "10afedd6-ff7f-51fa-bc1d-464cb204e6b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-{e}^{-2t}\\,j-2{e}^{-t/2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387904} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb8b86f-001a-5eb1-9ded-dead76cc9891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,i-2{e}^{-t}\\,j-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-t/2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387905} {:answer/id #uuid "ea538a96-8b67-5fc4-ba6a-05f6aa91f674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-2{e}^{-2t}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t/2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387906} {:answer/id #uuid "31024369-16ff-579a-acb7-e67065ff9581" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-2{e}^{2t}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea538a96-8b67-5fc4-ba6a-05f6aa91f674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,i-2{e}^{-2t}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t/2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387906} :answer-field/id #uuid "93216f8a-001b-5ecf-87cd-938ff9643b14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "629c6742-cb38-552f-bd6e-09f3aee65a84" :question/math-academy-id "q-128561" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\,i+{u}^{2}\\,j+\\sqrt{u}\\,k$ and $u(t)={e}^{-t},$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\sqrt{u})k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\,k \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})=-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t))\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u(t)}}\\,k)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{{e}^{-t}}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{e}^{-t}}}\\,k)\\cdot (-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =({e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{-t}\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{t/2}\\,k)\\cdot (-{e}^{-t}) \\\\  & =-\\,i-2{e}^{-2t}\\,j-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t/2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6770c6c3-ca44-5901-927f-1f6eb9c2f483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387910} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f467ee-f10f-5e09-b08f-f8641934f5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387911} {:answer/id #uuid "375265a8-c029-5e99-9d9a-45d5e93a7d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387912} {:answer/id #uuid "78262439-79b2-52fc-a07a-ed5fa9d567e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387913} {:answer/id #uuid "b4369e5c-dffe-55df-9352-d2f0194bfc84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "375265a8-c029-5e99-9d9a-45d5e93a7d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387912} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8592051-0273-5e7f-9289-65035199769c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "00ec801b-e22a-5c19-899f-45b6911ab4a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128570" :question/problem "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\left(\\frac{1}{u}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ec8602-0288-50f5-9393-d24f3e9978eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{6},\\,{t}^{5}+4{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387973} {:answer/id #uuid "059c4a79-58ba-5ab8-812b-f1ffa1abcd8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{6}-5,\\,4{t}^{5}+2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387974} {:answer/id #uuid "22face6d-6d51-591d-a1b9-744a0e476e64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{6}+1,\\,4{t}^{5},\\,{t}^{3}-5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387975} {:answer/id #uuid "8428706c-8f90-591b-9287-63282825708a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387976} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb7b979-4cab-5af0-b6ed-092b5e887c5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7{t}^{6},\\,6{t}^{5}-5,\\,4{t}^{3}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8428706c-8f90-591b-9287-63282825708a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387976} :answer-field/id #uuid "658bfb28-3b3a-5fa6-937f-fc8138b0b72f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c21f1368-688b-50ed-bde8-7422d801bdbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-128896" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨t,\\,5,\\,{t}^{4}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3} & t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & t\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & t\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩, \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ t & 5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}t & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}t & 5 \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩+⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9f86cd3-7815-52c3-a642-88091b5dca5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20t-2,\\,36{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390739} {:answer/id #uuid "3f10ad58-86c7-5488-87e8-2405ac572b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8t-2,\\,-48{t}^{2}+12t,\\,36{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390740} {:answer/id #uuid "b218608b-b05e-57e2-a7b7-ae74abf570fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨48t-2,\\,-362{t}^{2}+12t,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390741} {:answer/id #uuid "a3285904-7a37-5bb0-9e4b-ea28118d456b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-28t,\\,-24{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390742} {:answer/id #uuid "df14411c-6285-5ce6-9d91-f5503ce280c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-20t-2,\\,-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df14411c-6285-5ce6-9d91-f5503ce280c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-20t-2,\\,-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390743} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6adfc3-be4a-5dfa-b9ef-e4320cc373e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5c0ab63c-e0ff-5937-9e2f-94c308127204" :question/math-academy-id "q-32347" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨6{t}^{2},\\,2t,\\,6⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨3,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,4t-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12t,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 12t & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3{t}^{2} & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}12t & 0 \\\\ 3 & (4t-1)\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}12t & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨8t-2,\\,12t-48{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}-6⟩ \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6{t}^{2} & 2t & 6 \\\\ 0 & 6t & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2t & 6 \\\\ 6t & 4\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}6{t}^{2} & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}6{t}^{2} & 2t \\\\ 0 & 6t\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨-28t,\\,-24{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =⟨8t-2,\\,12t-48{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}-6⟩+⟨-28t,\\,-24{t}^{2},\\,36{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20t-2,\\,-72{t}^{2}+12t,\\,72{t}^{3}-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5e5d9ac-8a14-5201-9516-829a7b45050d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390800} {:answer/id #uuid "6ea13000-9bcb-54fe-a381-f6223d0bb92f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390801} {:answer/id #uuid "37229cb1-9b3d-541c-ad4c-f9ff6d2bee90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390802} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f3c695-f3a3-58d0-9e05-5aa5b210d1ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2+2t\\,,\\,-6t+8{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390803} {:answer/id #uuid "2452df56-9f06-5ed0-821f-9ea53a5fecf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37229cb1-9b3d-541c-ad4c-f9ff6d2bee90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390802} :answer-field/id #uuid "b00615b6-9721-5844-9bad-568a5f743f33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d806e973-4767-5c33-a683-2e2483aec09e" :question/math-academy-id "q-32836" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨1-{t}^{2}\\,,\\,1-{t}^{3}\\,,\\,1-t⟩$, find $({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t\\,,\\,-3{t}^{2}\\,,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\,,\\,-6t\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t)\\times f(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-6t & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{3} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-t\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -6t \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} & 1-{t}^{3}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {f}^{′}(t)\\times {f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3{t}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -3{t}^{2} & -1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-2t & -1 \\\\ -2t & -1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-2t & -3{t}^{2} \\\\ -2t & -3{t}^{2}\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\times f)^{′}(t) & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩+⟨0\\,,\\,0\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t+6{t}^{2}\\,,\\,2-2t\\,,\\,-2+6t-4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7eb18dc-1cd0-5f11-9766-9b39ce8627d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393003} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e290d0-94dc-5b31-a2bd-857a223edcdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ 1 \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393004} {:answer/id #uuid "79b7fc04-e9d4-5de3-8865-cddcf5f7acfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393005} {:answer/id #uuid "eecd81c6-e868-58ae-b147-24437027c490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393006} {:answer/id #uuid "01d87a17-578a-5627-9784-0c36eaa1beb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79b7fc04-e9d4-5de3-8865-cddcf5f7acfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393005} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bffeefe-923c-5235-a516-2e71c745f54b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d92bf36-e24a-53bf-b359-cf412f728c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-70688" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ -{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc0818f3-6660-5a5e-b58d-a575762526c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393010} {:answer/id #uuid "ab98f763-293f-5909-a542-20bf9e265d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393011} {:answer/id #uuid "fb1b744a-fd28-5436-8fa1-dc99d58a58de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393012} {:answer/id #uuid "0df38d96-3c28-5876-bdec-12fe8a88731c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ {e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393013} {:answer/id #uuid "978ffbca-fc6b-57e5-ac7d-a192ceaaf68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "978ffbca-fc6b-57e5-ac7d-a192ceaaf68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393014} :answer-field/id #uuid "198253e9-b22c-548e-8e45-872ef7aaca94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c43762c8-310f-5f86-a903-48bba629edc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70695" :question/problem "If $f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {u}^{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 3{u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ 3(u(t))^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u(t)}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3({e}^{t})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3d10de5-e9c5-5c37-aa64-fa06b54ead11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393107} {:answer/id #uuid "6cba95e3-79b8-5287-a813-d9e41cf5e8b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(t+3){e}^{3t} \\\\ (t+4){e}^{4t} \\\\ (t+5){e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393108} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a250be-c0e9-5cab-92c9-3d602707d998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5t{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393109} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7efc35-c9c9-54ba-9171-12ada5fa9705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}({t}^{2}+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2){e}^{4t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+3){e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393110} {:answer/id #uuid "d86e8688-766e-519c-8b4e-8b4b1b2281ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d86e8688-766e-519c-8b4e-8b4b1b2281ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393111} :answer-field/id #uuid "34376f88-2d0f-51e5-9b5f-462c8596e4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a49de4c-5d1f-5ca3-aa1a-4ebaca430818" :question/math-academy-id "q-71227" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=t.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{4t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{5t})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 5t{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(3t+1){e}^{3t} \\\\ (4t+1){e}^{4t} \\\\ (5t+1){e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9538c922-626d-57e3-875e-1c3a6b6e5675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(4{t}^{2}+t){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}-1){e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393114} {:answer/id #uuid "8c39359a-bdf1-5f7a-abe2-7ec39aa9faf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393115} {:answer/id #uuid "cd118cf1-a60f-5278-b6b0-774581fb4af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(-5{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (3{t}^{2}-t-1){e}^{t} \\\\ (t+2){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393116} {:answer/id #uuid "0231d3d9-379e-569f-8987-f29126252cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}({t}^{2}-4t+4) \\\\ ({t}^{2}-1) \\\\ (2t+3)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393117} {:answer/id #uuid "52e3e13a-2c9a-5dea-92ad-1d1be14d9577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c39359a-bdf1-5f7a-abe2-7ec39aa9faf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393115} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5faccf8-2ac3-56c6-9185-9f48d31adb8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c08c320-55ed-59e1-87a0-c92a722748de" :question/math-academy-id "q-71233" :question/problem "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ {t}^{2}+1 \\\\ 4t-7\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-7)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}2{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ {t}^{2}+1 \\\\ 4t-7\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}6{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(2{t}^{3}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-7){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 4{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141f5551-934e-5440-8953-1b3d3cf88e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i+12 e^{4 t}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532866} {:answer/id #uuid "44aab5b3-a627-5319-b75d-247ebb8b0162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6 - 9 t^{2})\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} - \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532874} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6b1f0d-8766-51a0-9b69-2576acc19597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t^{3} + 6 t + 3)\\,i+\\frac{3 \\left(\\left(t + 2\\right) e^{4 t} - 1\\right)}{t + 2}\\,j+6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532879} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2d1687-1eb8-5477-9fad-53c4f1a5c47a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532897} {:answer/id #uuid "fa448647-c439-5d87-9345-4f25b8d6061c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb2d1687-1eb8-5477-9fad-53c4f1a5c47a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532897} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b16c366-2ff9-5f7d-bf99-55f090fe22ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0ea031d4-a7c9-52a4-913c-d764f5dca240" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $3f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(t^{3} + 2)\\,i- \\frac{1}{t + 2}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(2 t - 1)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3f(t)+3g(t))'=3f'(\\!t)+3g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{3} + 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{1}{t + 2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=3 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=2\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3f(t)+3g(t))'&=3f'(\\!t)+3g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=3\\left(3 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+3\\left(2\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(6\\,i+12 e^{4 t}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e97975-4c74-5507-b653-606d0d1bf2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532868} {:answer/id #uuid "66c548d2-02d8-5526-b8e1-1c99ae671173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532880} {:answer/id #uuid "86ed3a70-cdde-56de-b810-9899566e914d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532887} {:answer/id #uuid "eed0e2f3-ee96-5a6d-a583-fb4c12616f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 8 t^{2} + 2 t - 10)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t - 3\\right) e^{4 t} + 4\\right)}{t - 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532906} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7037f7-a559-5d3e-be45-91f41c699e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16 t + 2)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66c548d2-02d8-5526-b8e1-1c99ae671173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532880} :answer-field/id #uuid "468a0c5a-ad2b-5b7f-abac-b961a5396963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "20b4dae3-6b9d-5ae1-bd0a-7100a3030dee" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(4 t^{2} + 1)\\,i- \\frac{4}{t - 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(t - 4)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t^{2} + 1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{4}{t - 3}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=1\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(1\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(2\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105fc45b-d9aa-5647-8478-24ee897554e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532865} {:answer/id #uuid "a392fa70-156d-57e7-82f2-0893b7b7ab65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-108,\\,3,\\,-252⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532892} {:answer/id #uuid "c18dca8f-f976-58fb-937e-0955da836ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24,\\,19,\\,48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532900} {:answer/id #uuid "d09c0c53-ad7d-5a79-92c3-cda91d610220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-36,\\,0,\\,-144⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532902} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d46704-3cf7-544d-aa5b-932780b205a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨72,\\,-3,\\,108⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105fc45b-d9aa-5647-8478-24ee897554e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532865} :answer-field/id #uuid "230e9f4b-ec6e-5a43-aa1f-9d2f50c7feb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "531c6c00-7c33-51fe-bcdf-6ff4d87bd71d" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle h(t)= ⟨6 t^{2},\\,3 - t,\\,3 t^{3} + 24⟩; g(t)= ⟨3 t \\left(t + 2\\right),\\,-8,\\,6 t^{3}⟩\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3h(t)-2g(t))'=3h'(\\!t)-2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6 t^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 - t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 24)⟩ \\\\ &=⟨12 t,\\,-1,\\,9 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t \\left(t + 2\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-8),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6 t^{3})⟩ \\\\ &=⟨6 t + 6,\\,0,\\,18 t^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3h(t)-2g(t))'\\big|_{t=2}&=3h'(\\!2)-2g'(\\!2) \\\\ &=3\\left(⟨24,\\,-1,\\,36⟩\\right)-2\\left(⟨18,\\,0,\\,72⟩\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(⟨72,\\,-3,\\,108⟩\\right)+\\left(⟨-36,\\,0,\\,-144⟩\\right) \\\\ &=⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f3c848-dbff-5f1b-ad1b-23f4831d8ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532862} {:answer/id #uuid "0c89cfd6-cb3c-558c-a04b-8bfe30bf8644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24,\\,-9,\\,-72⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532863} {:answer/id #uuid "19302086-6cf1-5118-9c0d-909000840d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,0,\\,96⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532867} {:answer/id #uuid "5aea8fe7-71be-55cc-b3e6-e7535c8fb3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,57,\\,-32⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532878} {:answer/id #uuid "eec84841-0dae-5761-b467-ce2eb2342da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-36,\\,9,\\,168⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07f3c848-dbff-5f1b-ad1b-23f4831d8ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532862} :answer-field/id #uuid "7288ecef-567e-595a-b90c-71125b365b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a68d13f-8399-5ff1-b774-b1b84a373282" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle h(t)= ⟨2 t^{2},\\,9 - 3 t,\\,- 2 t^{3} - 16⟩; g(t)= ⟨t \\left(t + 2\\right),\\,-24,\\,- 4 t^{3}⟩\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3h(t)-2g(t))'=3h'(\\!t)-2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9 - 3 t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t^{3} - 16)⟩ \\\\ &=⟨4 t,\\,-3,\\,- 6 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\left(t + 2\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-24),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t^{3})⟩ \\\\ &=⟨2 t + 2,\\,0,\\,- 12 t^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3h(t)-2g(t))'\\big|_{t=2}&=3h'(\\!2)-2g'(\\!2) \\\\ &=3\\left(⟨8,\\,-3,\\,-24⟩\\right)-2\\left(⟨6,\\,0,\\,-48⟩\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(⟨24,\\,-9,\\,-72⟩\\right)+\\left(⟨-12,\\,0,\\,96⟩\\right) \\\\ &=⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2592c444-2abd-56c3-9730-56a494189a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532872} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f57fdd-7ab8-5ee9-bfdd-4e1c04109c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532893} {:answer/id #uuid "aa480904-ff84-518d-9207-ac8579b1dfa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 12 t^{2})\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532894} {:answer/id #uuid "abcbc025-80ba-5616-8a44-cda642191303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 t^{3} + 8 t + 4)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{4 t} - 2\\right)}{t - 1}\\,j+4 \\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532895} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5d88ac-cf94-5f91-89c9-923fa247b61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9f57fdd-7ab8-5ee9-bfdd-4e1c04109c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532893} :answer-field/id #uuid "93b0a0f6-d902-5422-9a0c-2f37556f6f7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "709685a4-0960-5ef6-9050-4e687533ef07" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(2 t^{3} + 4)\\,i- \\frac{2}{t - 1}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(4 t - 2)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(2f(t)+2g(t))'=2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{3} + 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t - 1}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=6 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t - 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=4\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+2g(t))'&=2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=2\\left(6 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(4\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(12 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(8\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05042b03-df4c-5ccd-a964-8eaf6131a969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532861} {:answer/id #uuid "1c3aff9f-c826-5930-ba16-3983961fdd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532869} {:answer/id #uuid "838a64ec-997e-5f8b-96bd-2d63e5eac034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 t^{2}\\,i- \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532885} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0d38a-bfd3-57c3-907f-f60c0eb825dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 6 t^{3} + 8 t - 14)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t + 3\\right) e^{2 t} + 3\\right)}{t + 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532890} {:answer/id #uuid "bf993974-3b0c-5c9f-886d-1d6ca421c69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} + \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c3aff9f-c826-5930-ba16-3983961fdd31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532869} :answer-field/id #uuid "f573ff47-df7f-5224-8ed0-621e1426dd66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8facb5d0-2042-58b2-9944-895664b71392" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(3 t^{3} + 4)\\,i- \\frac{3}{t + 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(4 t - 3)\\,i+e^{2 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{3}{t + 3}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t - 3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=4\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(4\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 18 t^{2}\\,i- \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(8\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "777522b1-6939-5b66-8d41-4c0af7a31559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532884} {:answer/id #uuid "8631399e-befe-5fda-89cf-04216c222ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532886} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ccd2c1-ee5e-53ce-8fa5-271cd400ba26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 8 t^{2} + 4 t - 12)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t + 3\\right) e^{2 t} + 4\\right)}{t + 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532896} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9aa792-0b2d-537e-877a-bee6cb6606f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16 t + 4)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} + \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532898} {:answer/id #uuid "dd248600-23aa-53ba-92c5-dd1baf90dce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8631399e-befe-5fda-89cf-04216c222ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532886} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e314097-0298-520f-9c83-0f0fe71e1ac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a2b09545-4d92-5fd4-a34e-ae79048ac39c" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(4 t^{2} + 2)\\,i- \\frac{4}{t + 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(2 t - 4)\\,i+e^{2 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t^{2} + 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{4}{t + 3}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=2\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(2\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(4\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c25b5e8-29a2-5d6a-9195-b39381be0aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 + \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 3 t^{2} e^{t} - 9 t e^{t} - 6 e^{t} \\\\ 1 - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541245} {:answer/id #uuid "87e2b961-8e87-550d-a8e0-0ee0a3e468f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 t + 2 + \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 3 t^{2} e^{t} - 3 t e^{t} - 3 e^{t} \\\\ -1 - \\frac{1}{t} - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541249} {:answer/id #uuid "9a77f260-9187-5326-8c4a-24a29bc84c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 6 t e^{t} - 3 e^{t} \\\\ 2 + \\frac{1}{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541253} {:answer/id #uuid "a0404454-ff13-50be-8ab6-15207e83bcf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 + \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 6 t e^{t} - 3 e^{t} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{t} - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541254} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a7ebb6-60db-5509-bee6-228908d07bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 - \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ 3 t^{2} e^{t} - 3 t e^{t} \\\\ 3 + \\frac{2}{t} + \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c25b5e8-29a2-5d6a-9195-b39381be0aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 + \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 3 t^{2} e^{t} - 9 t e^{t} - 6 e^{t} \\\\ 1 - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541245} :answer-field/id #uuid "907eeef4-8e8b-5f0c-8e61-37d6501dc067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "14f8b19c-03b3-520d-8d8f-1445fd24196c" :question/problem "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=t^{2} + t + 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}=u^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t)f^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $u^{′}(t)$ and $f^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{′}(t)&=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 e^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 3 e^{t} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\u^{′}(t)&=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2} + t + 1)=2 t + 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′}&=u^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t)f^{′}(t)\\\\&=(2 t + 1)\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t}\\end{bmatrix}+(t^{2} + t + 1)\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ - 3 e^{t} \\\\ - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right) \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 \\left(2 t + 1\\right) e^{t} \\\\ \\frac{2 t + 1}{t}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\left(t^{2} + t + 1\\right)}{t} \\\\ - 3 \\left(t^{2} + t + 1\\right) e^{t} \\\\ - \\frac{t^{2} + t + 1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{bmatrix}4 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 t + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 + \\frac{2}{t} \\\\ 3 \\left(- t^{2} - 3 t - 2\\right) e^{t} \\\\ 1 - \\frac{1}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choice