selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3e6b721e-48c1-5f70-8c99-f141a075b6fb" :question/problem "Find $\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}$, where\n\n$$\nu(t)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)},\\qquad \\mathbf f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 t^{3} \\\\ - 2 t^{2} \\\\ - 2 t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume $t>0$." :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=u^{\\prime}(t)\\mathbf f(t)+u(t)\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the scalar and each vector component.\n\n$$\nu^{\\prime}(t)=- \\frac{2}{t}.\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} \\\\ - 4 t \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute both contributions and add corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}&=\\big(- \\frac{2}{t}\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 t^{3} \\\\ - 2 t^{2} \\\\ - 2 t\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} \\\\ - 4 t \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite $\\mathbf h(t)=u(t)\\mathbf f(t)$. For each component, the two terms are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_{1}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(4 t^{2}\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(12 t^{2} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\big)\\\\&=12 t^{2} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 t^{2}\\\\h_{2}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(4 t\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(8 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\big)\\\\&=8 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 t\\\\h_{3}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(4\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\big)\\\\&=4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}12 t^{2} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 t^{2} \\\\ 8 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 t \\\\ 4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02645125-edbe-5f98-b3cf-c819fee2ad49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 4 t \\\\ 4 t + 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723340} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1c05da-9280-54cb-a139-d77c4691c92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ - 4 t - 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723345} {:answer/id #uuid "9b09f245-4765-56fe-b5ae-ee6e63b599cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ - 2 t - 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723358} {:answer/id #uuid "b408cf2a-f332-5fa6-86a3-80e6947d002f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 8 t^{2} + 8 t \\\\ - 4 t - 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723364} {:answer/id #uuid "b8482b4d-90db-518c-b0a0-bd9e40a071b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e1c05da-9280-54cb-a139-d77c4691c92c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ - 4 t - 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723345} :answer-field/id #uuid "faf9cc6b-47f0-5d61-9ec6-1b626b7e3bc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5ca41269-6938-5083-b716-5a823f41c34e" :question/problem "Find $\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}$, where\n\n$$\nu(t)=- t - 1,\\qquad \\mathbf f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ - 2 t^{2} \\\\ 2 t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=u^{\\prime}(t)\\mathbf f(t)+u(t)\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the scalar and each vector component.\n\n$$\nu^{\\prime}(t)=-1.\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ - 4 t \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute both contributions and add corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}&=\\big(-1\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ - 2 t^{2} \\\\ 2 t\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- t - 1\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ - 4 t \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite $\\mathbf h(t)=u(t)\\mathbf f(t)$. For each component, the two terms are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_{1}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(2\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(0\\big)\\\\&=2\\\\h_{2}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(2 t^{2}\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 4 t \\left(- t - 1\\right)\\big)\\\\&=6 t^{2} + 4 t\\\\h_{3}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(- 2 t\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 2 t - 2\\big)\\\\&=- 4 t - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ - 4 t - 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0558599b-b092-5578-b4bf-9ea105a81ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - 12 t^{2} \\\\ - 2 t - 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723341} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0ec268-9d6a-5755-8dd2-16aa287972fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 t^{3} \\\\ - 2 t \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723343} {:answer/id #uuid "56bbf595-d936-5dc2-ba62-ba7f29d1866d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 20 t^{3} - 12 t^{2} \\\\ - 6 t - 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723349} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8e82e4-361a-55ba-823d-4819dc65886c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 16 t^{3} - 12 t^{2} \\\\ - 4 t - 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723359} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4b07fb-2d3e-5a46-b30a-d5a056776241" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 20 t^{3} - 24 t^{2} \\\\ - 2 t - 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e8e82e4-361a-55ba-823d-4819dc65886c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 16 t^{3} - 12 t^{2} \\\\ - 4 t - 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723359} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5e50acd-4212-513d-86b4-403e60672a1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b63c0962-e255-50eb-b3e5-99982746be24" :question/problem "Find $\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}$, where\n\n$$\nu(t)=- 2 t - 2,\\qquad \\mathbf f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 t^{3} \\\\ t \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=u^{\\prime}(t)\\mathbf f(t)+u(t)\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the scalar and each vector component.\n\n$$\nu^{\\prime}(t)=-2.\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 t^{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute both contributions and add corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}&=\\big(-2\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}2 t^{3} \\\\ t \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 2 t - 2\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}6 t^{2} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite $\\mathbf h(t)=u(t)\\mathbf f(t)$. For each component, the two terms are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_{1}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(- 4 t^{3}\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(6 t^{2} \\left(- 2 t - 2\\right)\\big)\\\\&=- 16 t^{3} - 12 t^{2}\\\\h_{2}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(- 2 t\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 2 t - 2\\big)\\\\&=- 4 t - 2\\\\h_{3}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(2\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(0\\big)\\\\&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}- 16 t^{3} - 12 t^{2} \\\\ - 4 t - 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d1a853e-d74a-5959-ac81-f3454679d6a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} + 8 t \\\\ -2 \\\\ t - 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723342} {:answer/id #uuid "41db50da-2011-5469-b0da-6eaf612047e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 t^{2} - 4 t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723348} {:answer/id #uuid "7b41a8ca-8abe-5f5c-b5b6-dca0ce188b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 t^{2} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723354} {:answer/id #uuid "b3657f78-c7ab-51d3-8e51-244121ea0d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 t - 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723363} {:answer/id #uuid "e41eda27-4917-502d-8d98-edb1869b2ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ 0 \\\\ t - 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3657f78-c7ab-51d3-8e51-244121ea0d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 t - 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723363} :answer-field/id #uuid "8253a4c6-81ed-5ecd-a0a9-5d4af0dc0611" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f272166b-dd95-52d4-a80e-2ca241ea9704" :question/problem "Find $\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}$, where\n\n$$\nu(t)=t - 1,\\qquad \\mathbf f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 t^{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=u^{\\prime}(t)\\mathbf f(t)+u(t)\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t).\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the scalar and each vector component.\n\n$$\nu^{\\prime}(t)=1.\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f^{\\prime}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute both contributions and add corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}&=\\big(1\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 t^{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&\\quad+\\big(t - 1\\big)\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite $\\mathbf h(t)=u(t)\\mathbf f(t)$. For each component, the two terms are:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h_{1}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(- 2 t^{2}\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(- 4 t \\left(t - 1\\right)\\big)\\\\&=- 6 t^{2} + 4 t\\\\h_{2}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(2\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(0\\big)\\\\&=2\\\\h_{3}^{\\prime}(t)&=\\big(t\\big)\\\\&\\quad+\\big(t - 1\\big)\\\\&=2 t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t)\\mathbf f(t)\\big)^{\\prime}=\\begin{bmatrix}- 6 t^{2} + 4 t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 t - 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723404 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0325466f-edd0-55eb-87f3-81582c16ba75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ 16 \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723405} {:answer/id #uuid "06efebf1-92b6-54db-8c9d-59222944917d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723406} {:answer/id #uuid "45eb2df7-73f5-52a8-a021-aa3f28ef6121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723419} {:answer/id #uuid "c2237ece-66af-592d-970b-4994d500ec8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723431} {:answer/id #uuid "e18dbf9d-9105-52ca-b87b-058f6639c6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2237ece-66af-592d-970b-4994d500ec8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723431} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c3d5eae-7e01-5beb-81c5-4f1fecd2c1b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "01e9707f-50bd-5552-9b55-4f565017cb29" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}e^{u} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(u \\right)} \\\\ \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=4 t - 3$. Find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer function component by component and the scalar inner function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f'(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}e^{u} \\\\ - \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ u'(t) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the inner input and multiply **every component** by the same scalar derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t) & =\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot\\left(4\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 e^{4 t - 3} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)} \\\\ 4 \\cos{\\left(4 t - 3 \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProducts and reciprocals of exponential factors simplify by adding or subtracting their exponents."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00031ab0-a34b-5482-b435-825e7b7491ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ \\frac{9 e^{\\frac{9 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723403} {:answer/id #uuid "73201250-c63a-5142-8fb3-eaf30e01763d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ - \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723424} {:answer/id #uuid "88a2949b-9ba3-5e2d-87e1-ace73b9f3f53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ - \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 9 e^{3 t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723426} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bdc3c0-ac55-5299-bf4e-ef4fda00b366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 9 e^{3 t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723436} {:answer/id #uuid "fa378b51-267c-530c-b306-73ee9f2419dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa378b51-267c-530c-b306-73ee9f2419dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723437} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd5b96e-5c21-57ac-8992-019372621921" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723433}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "116704d3-2911-595d-bb66-c79997eab4d1" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{u} \\\\ \\ln{\\left(u \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=e^{3 t}$. Find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer function component by component and the scalar inner function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f'(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 u \\\\ \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{u}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ u'(t) & =3 e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the inner input and multiply **every component** by the same scalar derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t) & =\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 e^{3 t} \\\\ \\frac{e^{- \\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ e^{- 3 t}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot\\left(3 e^{3 t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 e^{6 t} \\\\ \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{3 t}{2}}}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProducts and reciprocals of exponential factors simplify by adding or subtracting their exponents. Here $u(t)>0$. Taking the square root of a positive exponential halves its exponent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fecfba0-e87c-58b4-9b0e-ec22bcc9564e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ e^{- t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723415} {:answer/id #uuid "42743b31-fa0c-5369-8ebc-9187eb08a858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723417} {:answer/id #uuid "5950a0b5-e839-506d-96e0-156f0bd62b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723420} {:answer/id #uuid "5de94bf5-9240-5012-867d-5eb3be46bbe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ - \\frac{e^{- t}}{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723422} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c6322b-7afe-505e-ad71-2bc2ac04b1a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ e^{- t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5950a0b5-e839-506d-96e0-156f0bd62b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723420} :answer-field/id #uuid "231fd02b-f4c5-5db4-a99c-cbdff1196afd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "18cf5c63-7cb4-5e47-a787-1bcd712bfa9c" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos{\\left(u \\right)} \\\\ u^{3} \\\\ \\ln{\\left(u \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=e^{- t}$. Find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer function component by component and the scalar inner function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f'(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}- \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\\\ 3 u^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ u'(t) & =- e^{- t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the inner input and multiply **every component** by the same scalar derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t) & =\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}- \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ 3 e^{- 2 t} \\\\ e^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot\\left(- e^{- t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}e^{- t} \\sin{\\left(e^{- t} \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{- 3 t} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProducts and reciprocals of exponential factors simplify by adding or subtracting their exponents. Here $u(t)>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723416 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122d668f-50a0-5652-a405-d7a146ea2ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 8 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ - 4 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723408} {:answer/id #uuid "23886f43-530b-5fba-b7fb-e877cc011800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 16 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723412} {:answer/id #uuid "76af7215-9492-5575-abd4-a9cd93e4aa2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 8 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ 16 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723425} {:answer/id #uuid "9b14eb5a-e468-51af-a573-738997b50916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ - 4 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723428} {:answer/id #uuid "eb23dd55-0b09-520f-af2e-1543c97d328f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 8 t e^{- 4 t} \\\\ - 4 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "122d668f-50a0-5652-a405-d7a146ea2ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 8 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ - 4 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723408} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b53f5fa-9e1d-5631-8500-f6704b36588c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "38b3e7d9-3fea-5fdc-98c2-96b17af0d7af" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} \\\\ u \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=e^{- 4 t}$. Find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer function component by component and the scalar inner function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f'(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 u \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ u'(t) & =- 4 e^{- 4 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the inner input and multiply **every component** by the same scalar derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t) & =\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot\\left(- 4 e^{- 4 t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 8 e^{- 8 t} \\\\ - 4 e^{- 4 t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProducts and reciprocals of exponential factors simplify by adding or subtracting their exponents. Here $u(t)>0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b1a9866-5f4e-5952-b094-daebef88bd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{8 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723413} {:answer/id #uuid "2f51d4f9-d94a-5722-ab55-a56652a89737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{16 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723414} {:answer/id #uuid "445edc25-36ce-5793-ad48-071b7defee04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723418} {:answer/id #uuid "6160039b-d5c9-5e6b-9459-2a167eee4730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{8 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723423} {:answer/id #uuid "8f368ab4-01f4-50fa-99f5-1ed04d0d63a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6160039b-d5c9-5e6b-9459-2a167eee4730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{8 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723423} :answer-field/id #uuid "c667a2ad-40c7-543e-8339-d259bb3d5d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b1814f65-9028-5f66-8193-91b784fb09f1" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf f(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ u^{2} \\\\ \\ln{\\left(u \\right)}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$. Find $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)$. Work on the real domain $t>1$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer function component by component and the scalar inner function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f'(u) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 u \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ u'(t) & =\\frac{2}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the inner input and multiply **every component** by the same scalar derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t) & =\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{8 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3353c5-25db-5e97-9920-7001bdae531f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723510} {:answer/id #uuid "66414d4f-9055-51b9-b658-bbd4a383bc47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723514} {:answer/id #uuid "66de178e-45de-5414-a820-934d7814840b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723515} {:answer/id #uuid "d3146e6d-b03b-53dd-8cf8-05dbacf0f873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723533} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd77ec6-234f-5fde-8364-1d6bba8f35b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddd77ec6-234f-5fde-8364-1d6bba8f35b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723534} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ebe4e57-e99b-5bf9-bf1f-2926df70ece0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "007622f5-6ac1-58be-a7f1-e283e4ad64d5" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=(- t^{3} - 1)\\,i+(3 t^{2} + 3)\\,j+t^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- t^{3} - 1)=- 3 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} + 3)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- 3 t^{2}\\,i+6 t\\,j+2 t\\,k \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{2})=- 6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =- 6 t\\,i+6\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(0)(-1)+(6)(3)+(2)(0) \\\\  & =18 \\\\ P_2 & =(0)(0)+(0)(0)+(0)(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(0) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a28a204-0450-5f5c-9198-1dc31250c07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 t^{3} + 4 t^{2} - 7 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723517} {:answer/id #uuid "9915a58e-2d48-5915-b557-79380a9e9bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t^{3} + t^{2} - 4 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723520} {:answer/id #uuid "be378b94-d574-5e84-8721-1aa15a6f1457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723528} {:answer/id #uuid "c30fe383-bb93-511b-bd16-f84f3cb024cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t^{3} - t^{2} + 4 t + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723529} {:answer/id #uuid "f5696126-d9c4-5849-ad09-e81b30fa674f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{3} + t^{2} - t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be378b94-d574-5e84-8721-1aa15a6f1457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723528} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac01c14b-740b-55de-95b4-9c89c5517e26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e115102-0aa3-579c-8fe1-b0154b41a4be" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(t - 2)\\,i- 2 t\\,j+t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(t^{2} + t)\\,i+t\\,j+t^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 2)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t)=-2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =\\,i-2\\,j+\\,k \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2} + t)=2 t + 1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2} \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =(2 t + 1)\\,i+\\,j+3 t^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(1)(t^{2} + t)+(-2)(t)+(1)(t^{3}) \\\\  & =t^{3} + t^{2} - t \\\\ P_2 & =(t - 2)(2 t + 1)+(- 2 t)(1)+(t)(3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =3 t^{3} + 2 t^{2} - 5 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =4 t^{3} + 3 t^{2} - 6 t - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c8d4d0-6598-58f1-b0e2-9d51af707ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\ln{(t )}}{2} + 6 + \\frac{6}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723507} {:answer/id #uuid "67bfc169-3d7a-5954-b380-7472539fb5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15 - 15 \\ln{(t )}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723516} {:answer/id #uuid "a0958627-c4d0-577f-b94a-1d5d64b7cdde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 21 \\ln{(t )} + 24 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723523} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b649e8-d4c8-5754-b06a-0719d726ffc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{t} - \\frac{4}{t^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723530} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf32613-c394-5977-8423-7a9d69bda73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf32613-c394-5977-8423-7a9d69bda73a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723539} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb3c891-1037-51e5-ae4a-de9fe646e4d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5998b21e-5a65-5da2-b4a5-40c888949f7f" :question/problem "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =- 3 \\ln{(t )}\\,i- 2 t\\,j+\\frac{2}{t}\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =- 3 t\\,i+3 \\ln{(t )}\\,j- \\frac{2}{t}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$ Assume $t>0$." :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 \\ln{(t )})=- \\frac{3}{t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t)=-2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)=- \\frac{2}{t^{2}} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- \\frac{3}{t}\\,i-2\\,j- \\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\,k \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t)=-3 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 \\ln{(t )})=\\frac{3}{t} \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\left(- \\frac{2}{t}\\right)=\\frac{2}{t^{2}} \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =-3\\,i+\\frac{3}{t}\\,j+\\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\left(- \\frac{3}{t}\\right)(- 3 t)+(-2)(3 \\ln{(t )})+\\left(- \\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\right)\\left(- \\frac{2}{t}\\right) \\\\  & =- 6 \\ln{(t )} + 9 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}} \\\\ P_2 & =(- 3 \\ln{(t )})(-3)+(- 2 t)\\left(\\frac{3}{t}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2}{t}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{t^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =9 \\ln{(t )} - 6 + \\frac{4}{t^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =3 \\ln{(t )} + 3 + \\frac{8}{t^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db647fc-327e-5438-b8f1-599f7685c3f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723508} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d5c244-c736-567a-8cff-ec98d19481b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27 t^{4} + 108 t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723526} {:answer/id #uuid "b5407feb-7290-5232-8611-9aeb0eeb2889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{135 t^{4}}{2} - 12 t^{2} - 27 t - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723527} {:answer/id #uuid "d08b7560-3aa2-5cfe-b8eb-cf6d655e7261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} - 54 t + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723532} {:answer/id #uuid "de5d6480-5898-5c9a-b2f6-37b2d1c04a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "189 t^{4} + 32 t^{2} + 108 t + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db647fc-327e-5438-b8f1-599f7685c3f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723508} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1591793-1f91-504a-b535-36ad122cf043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6fb23ec1-6e13-5a4a-bb47-de87e3f76c31" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨3 t^{3} + 3,\\,2 t,\\,2 t^{2} + 1⟩$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 3)=9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2} + 1)=4 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨9 t^{2},\\,2,\\,4 t⟩ \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(9 t^{2})=18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(4 t)=4 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =⟨18 t,\\,0,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(18 t)(3 t^{3} + 3)+(0)(2 t)+(4)(2 t^{2} + 1) \\\\  & =54 t^{4} + 8 t^{2} + 54 t + 4 \\\\ P_2 & =(9 t^{2})(9 t^{2})+(2)(2)+(4 t)(4 t) \\\\  & =81 t^{4} + 16 t^{2} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =135 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 54 t + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d7a9b0-ba6a-505f-b59f-c84934a2c22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723506} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9a292f-3140-5dbf-b551-d106374550ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162 t^{3} + 36 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723512} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe53a65-6f99-5361-b740-0bdb2edeb6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "81 t^{4} + 36 t^{2} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723531} {:answer/id #uuid "eaad29fe-f20e-5277-b2d4-e86403f7c23d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 270 t^{4} - 108 t^{2} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723536} {:answer/id #uuid "f2cb46ac-0c6c-573b-934d-92ac75107f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 27 t^{4} - 18 t^{2} - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09d7a9b0-ba6a-505f-b59f-c84934a2c22a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723506} :answer-field/id #uuid "4579a44b-0d5e-5193-a25f-3421dfe80149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9c1ef875-08ca-5c88-b962-6b2e6956080e" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=- 3 t^{3}\\,i+(3 t^{2} - 2)\\,j+2 t\\,k$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the dot product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\cdot f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\cdot f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{3})=- 9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} - 2)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)=2 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =- 9 t^{2}\\,i+6 t\\,j+2\\,k \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 9 t^{2})=- 18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =- 18 t\\,i+6\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(- 18 t)(- 3 t^{3})+(6)(3 t^{2} - 2)+(0)(2 t) \\\\  & =54 t^{4} + 18 t^{2} - 12 \\\\ P_2 & =(- 9 t^{2})(- 9 t^{2})+(6 t)(6 t)+(2)(2) \\\\  & =81 t^{4} + 36 t^{2} + 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\cdot f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =135 t^{4} + 54 t^{2} - 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4db2b3-e025-5f86-a8c1-bc0a73c35260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t,\\,54 t^{2},\\,-18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723544} {:answer/id #uuid "8df4a47f-a6cb-55a9-898d-1c779c8071ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,0,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723547} {:answer/id #uuid "bce9f74a-e285-562e-9dad-462de73c0bb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723550} {:answer/id #uuid "efa0f20f-ae68-5df5-a55e-e5c45eaa7b70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,18 t^{3} - 9 t + 9,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723552} {:answer/id #uuid "fad4f7a8-bb45-5ce8-bca3-9a113570021c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,72 t^{3} - 36 t + 36,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce9f74a-e285-562e-9dad-462de73c0bb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723550} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d54dfca-d4a3-53bf-970a-33dd4fd84dba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9816a80a-26f7-5ab7-b297-c498df4dd904" :question/problem "Given $f(t)=⟨3 t^{2} - 1,\\,- 3 t - 3,\\,3 t^{3} - 3⟩$, find $(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\times f(t)+f^{\\prime}(t)\\times f^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{2} - 1)=6 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t - 3)=-3 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t^{3} - 3)=9 t^{2} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨6 t,\\,-3,\\,9 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t)=6 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(-3)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(9 t^{2})=18 t \\\\ f^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =⟨6,\\,0,\\,18 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 0 & 18 t \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & - 3 t - 3 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 18 t \\\\ - 3 t - 3 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix}=54 t^{2} + 54 t \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 18 t \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & 3 t^{3} - 3\\end{vmatrix}=36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18 \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 3 t^{2} - 1 & - 3 t - 3\\end{vmatrix}=- 18 t - 18 \\\\ P_1 & =⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 6 t & -3 & 9 t^{2} \\\\ 6 t & -3 & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 9 t^{2} \\\\ -3 & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}6 t & 9 t^{2} \\\\ 6 t & 9 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}6 t & -3 \\\\ 6 t & -3\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_2 & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f^{\\prime}\\times f)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨54 t^{2} + 54 t,\\,36 t^{3} - 18 t + 18,\\,- 18 t - 18⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f17d1d-8cf8-5453-80ea-fbe416dc37b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723541} {:answer/id #uuid "0dbd55d7-a479-5387-a5e0-2f3161f3c66c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 48 t^{3} - 4 t - 2 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723542} {:answer/id #uuid "8360a287-0b05-53ca-89e7-37a5daa77a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t - 5 \\\\ 4 - 35 t \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723546} {:answer/id #uuid "b06e9db5-3071-5050-b9c4-458e1f4ec6e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 36 t^{3} - 3 t - 3 \\\\ 4 - 33 t \\\\ - 8 t^{2} - 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723549} {:answer/id #uuid "f37ec804-ae53-5709-b7fe-c2f9b03f8f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 18 t^{3} - \\frac{3 t}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 - \\frac{33 t}{2} \\\\ - 4 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03f17d1d-8cf8-5453-80ea-fbe416dc37b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723541} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b0c43f-8b5a-51cc-acab-2a83c6fc3b0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c129f4fb-82d5-5476-8c23-145c24dded8c" :question/problem "Find $(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 t^{2} \\\\ t + 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ g(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ t - 1 \\\\ - 3 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t)=f^{\\prime}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times g^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(-3)=0 \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2})=4 t \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t + 2)=1 \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 1)=1 \\\\ g^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t^{2})=- 6 t \\\\ g^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ - 6 t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 4 t & 1 \\\\ t & t - 1 & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 t & 1 \\\\ t - 1 & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=- 12 t^{3} - t + 1 \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ t & - 3 t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=t \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 t \\\\ t & t - 1\\end{vmatrix}=- 4 t^{2} \\\\ P_1 & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t + 1 \\\\ t \\\\ - 4 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 t^{2} & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 t^{2} & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix}=- 12 t^{3} - t - 2 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & t + 2 \\\\ 1 & - 6 t\\end{vmatrix}=2 - 17 t \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 t^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=- 2 t^{2} - 3 \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 12 t^{3} - t - 2 \\\\ 2 - 17 t \\\\ - 2 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 24 t^{3} - 2 t - 1 \\\\ 2 - 16 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b0e6f3a-a6f5-5a5b-8736-75504782a6db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,- 2 e^{4 t},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723556} {:answer/id #uuid "3da10f2d-2c58-5a1d-8caa-29f707c0a7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,- e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723557} {:answer/id #uuid "4a242423-8170-50dc-a558-0b9e7914f40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723558} {:answer/id #uuid "624d1e86-69a4-5774-a6d3-0bfdbf966bd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723559} {:answer/id #uuid "8766f12a-a624-5bba-bf10-8af18c52195e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a242423-8170-50dc-a558-0b9e7914f40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723558} :answer-field/id #uuid "856534c6-7179-5f48-b48e-329c9b3017b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0dc45519-249e-53bf-ad66-0c4633428e6f" :question/problem "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime}$ given that $f(t)=⟨e^{- t},\\,e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩$ and $v(t)=e^{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "Use the scalar function multiple rule:\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime}=v(t)f^{\\prime}(t)+v^{\\prime}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{- t})=- e^{- t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t})=3 e^{3 t} \\\\ f^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t + 3})=e^{t + 3} \\\\ f^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨- e^{- t},\\,3 e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\ v^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{t})=e^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =(e^{t})⟨- e^{- t},\\,3 e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,3 e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =(e^{t})⟨e^{- t},\\,e^{3 t},\\,e^{t + 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,e^{4 t},\\,e^{t} e^{t + 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{\\prime} & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4 e^{4 t},\\,2 e^{2 t + 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
